      "content": "It is completely understandable to feel depleted when you've been fighting this battle for so long; the exhaustion you feel is real. Please do not internalize this as a personal failing or proof that you are \"broken.\" Instead of focusing on \"fixing\" yourself, perhaps we can look at ways to build gentle support systems that acknowledge the difficulty of the journey. Reaching out to a professional who specializes in addiction can provide a different, more compassionate approach than what you may have experienced before.",
      "source": "target",
